spec: S18-06, S18-07, S18-09

Ticket 18 on the second server (profile `ios` = its owner @ana), started with
`--url http://pw-host.example.ts.net:7377 --link-base https://cd.example.dev`: `link` goes through
the relay (`{link_base}/{host:port}/d/{id}[#tN]`, no note), `show` on a TTY appends the same link
(non-TTY unchanged), and `pair` prints the `annotary://pair` URL (non-TTY: one line; TTY:
header, the QR code in quadrant blocks, `profile ana@pw-host`, the URL, and the shown-once note).
Tokens and ids are random, so they are `[..]`; the QR block is `...`. Merged stdout+stderr.

```console
$ annotary -p ios push ios-plan.md
ios-plan	[..]	v1

$ annotary -p ios thread new ios-plan --document -m "Take a look on your phone."
t1	document

$ annotary -p ios link ios-plan t1
https://cd.example.dev/pw-host.example.ts.net:7377/d/[..]#t1

$ ANNOTARY_TTY=1 NO_COLOR=1 annotary -p ios link ios-plan
https://cd.example.dev/pw-host.example.ts.net:7377/d/[..]

$ annotary -p ios link ios-plan t1 --json url,thread,public
{"url":"https://cd.example.dev/pw-host.example.ts.net:7377/d/[..]#t1","thread":"t1","public":true}

$ ANNOTARY_TTY=1 NO_COLOR=1 annotary -p ios show ios-plan
ios-plan  [..]  notes  v1 by @ana [..]  action:-  open:1  actions:approve,send-back  https://cd.example.dev/pw-host.example.ts.net:7377/d/[..]
...

$ annotary -p ios show ios-plan
ios-plan	[..]	notes	v1 by @ana [..]	action:-	open:1	actions:approve,send-back
...

$ annotary -p ios pair
annotary://pair?v=1&server=http%3A%2F%2Fpw-host.example.ts.net%3A7377&token=[..]&profile=ana%40pw-host	ana	[..]	device

$ ANNOTARY_TTY=1 NO_COLOR=1 annotary -p ios pair --name iPhone
Pairing a device for @ana on http://pw-host.example.ts.net:7377
...
profile ana@pw-host
annotary://pair?v=1&server=http%3A%2F%2Fpw-host.example.ts.net%3A7377&token=[..]&profile=ana%40pw-host
Shown once. Revoke: annotary token revoke [..]

$ annotary -p ios pair --json member,name,profile,server
{"member":"ana","name":"device","profile":"ana@pw-host","server":"http://pw-host.example.ts.net:7377"}

```
